  "_meta": {
    "description": "Golden fixture for check-role-drift.py. Expected shape (trust subjects, service principals, attached managed-policy ARNs, and inline-policy statement action/resource sets) for each of the 8 operational IAM roles, hand-derived from the legacy Terraform module -- NOT parsed from Terraform at runtime.",
    "reference_repo": "/Users/antoniopm61data/pm61data/iac-terraform-install-redesign",
    "reference_repo_note": "All 'source' paths below are relative to reference_repo, i.e. 'modules/iam_oidc/x.tf' means '<reference_repo>/aws/infrastructure/modules/iam_oidc/x.tf'. locals.tf and variables.tf are at '<reference_repo>/aws/infrastructure/{locals,variables}.tf'.",
    "derived_on": "2026-08-20",
    "regenerate_when": "module.iam_oidc/*.tf, modules/iam/*.tf, or locals.tf's role_config in the reference repo change. Re-read the cited source lines, re-derive trust_subjects/service_principals/managed_policy_arns/statements for the affected role(s), and update both the JSON and the 'source' citation if line numbers moved.",
    "normalization_applied_by_script": [
      "1. RoleName is never read from either side -- roles are matched by CloudFormation logical ID / Terraform resource, not by the generated name string.",
      "2. KMS Resource: any 'arn:aws:kms:<region>:<account>:key/<anything>' collapses to 'arn:aws:kms:*:*:key/*' on both sides (customer-CFT convention == TF's scoped ebs_kms_key_arn/kms_key_id).",
      "3. Region/account/partition placeholders (${AWS::Region}/${AWS::AccountId} and TF's data.aws_region.current.*/data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id) collapse to '*' on both sides.",
      "4. GlueTrinoServiceRole's self-referential iam:PassRole resource (it passes itself to glue.amazonaws.com) collapses to 'arn:aws:iam::*:role/<SELF>' -- this is rule 1 applied to a Resource value rather than a RoleName property."
    ],
    "known_caveats": [
      "PGBackupServiceRole trust_subjects below (4 subjects, matching foundation.yaml) are derived from modules/iam_oidc/pgbackup-cj-oidc.tf's dynamic 'system:serviceaccount:${ns}:sa-ecr-registry' loop over the ROOT var.cronjob_namespaces DEFAULT (variables.tf:289-293, default = [\"intelligentedge\", \"rasa\", \"cluster-management\"]) plus its hardcoded intelligentedge:s3-backup-sa subject -- NOT from locals.tf's role_config.pg_backup_cronjob_oidc_role_arn, which is STALE: it hardcodes only 3 namespace/sa_name pairs (intelligentedge/sa-ecr-registry, cluster-management/sa-ecr-registry, intelligentedge/s3-backup-sa) and is missing a 'rasa' entry entirely (locals.tf:41-45). That role_config feeds module.modify_iam_oidc_role_trust_policy, the trust-PATCH path Terraform runs against BYO (foundation.yaml-created) roles post-cluster-creation -- so as written today, the reference repo's own trust-patch would silently drop the rasa grant it it ever ran against a real BYO PGBackupServiceRole. Flagged separately (not this script's concern -- it's an inconsistency inside the TF reference, not a CFT-vs-TF drift); see the spawned follow-up task. This script's baseline intentionally follows the 4-subject (cronjob_namespaces-derived) version because it is what the *directly-created* role gets, it is internally consistent with variables.tf's own default, and it is what foundation.yaml already matches."
    ]
  },
